Comment to what extent the outputs have been achieved. Comment on the activities that have taken place and the most important milestones.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <actual value="Covid has slowed down project progress hoping for the practical Foundation Training to be delivered in NW-Uganda - this has not materialized necessitating the development of alternatives (such as online meetings and facilitation and development of web-based learning materials). These however add the need for training and research into the best methods and tools. This has not fundamentally affected project deliverables, both outputs, and outcomes. Throughout the year, there were bi-weekly meetings to capture learning needs and coordinate amongst partners. Participants for the Foundation Course were selected strategically. Moreover, the Foundation Course was developed (web-based) and is to start end of July.  The bi-weekly meetings served as a platform to strengthen cooperation amongst partners, as well as they were practically useful to discuss for example logistics related to participants&apos; travel and visas. Getting visas for staff from Somaliland to travel to NW Uganda proved very difficult! Strategies were developed to contextualize the Foundation Course in such ways that it will ease the design and delivery of In-Country Courses."></actual>
